<title>FRANCE: Cerus shares requote at 133 francs in Paris.</title>
<headline>Cerus shares requote at 133 francs in Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cerus requoted at 133 francs ($26.09) at 0840 GMT, up 11.95 percent from Friday's close, after a newspaper report that CGIP was in talks to buy out Cerus, Italian industrialist Carlo De Benedetti's French holding company.</p>
<p>The stock was suspended limit-up twice earlier.</p>
<p>CGIP and Cerus both declined to comment on the report in the newspaper Les Echos.</p>
<p>Shares in CGIP were down 20 francs at 1,190.</p>
<p>Cerus holds 28 percent of car parts manufacturer Valeo, whose stock was down 4.70 francs at 275 at 0845 GMT.</p>
<p>($ = 5.097 French Francs)</p>
</text>
